        "paragraphs": [
          "Ask for the source length, expected deliverables, review contact, deadline and number of revision rounds. Confirm who supplies scripts, captions, brand assets and music, and who checks permission to use them. Identify the approved file-transfer route and the person authorized to provide direction. If several people can request changes independently, ask the team to consolidate feedback before you begin. Conflicting instructions consume time and can leave nobody willing to approve the result.",
          "Separate the initial agreement from later requests. For example, a brief for one captioned announcement does not automatically include five additional versions, a new script or account publishing. Discuss compensation and delivery conditions before accepting the project, with any change process recorded. You can offer a smaller paid test when both parties need evidence of working fit. The test should have a defined purpose and agreed use, just like a larger assignment."
        ]
