          "For that practice announcement, you could send a review copy, collect one consolidated note, deliver the revised versions and ask for written approval. At handoff, list the filenames, dimensions and any remaining limitations. Confirm how long you will retain working files and what you will delete according to the agreement. Do not promise permanent storage unless you have deliberately arranged and priced that responsibility.",
          "Include a separate accuracy pass before handoff. Check names against the approved reference, read captions without relying on the audio and confirm that the final export matches the reviewed version. If the client supplies a correction after approval, identify whether it is a factual fix or a new creative request and agree how to handle it. These checks show an employer how you protect the details that a fast showreel cannot demonstrate.",
