          "Send a short agenda if nobody has provided one. Put the main question first, followed by the information needed to answer it and the next-step decision. An illustrative half-hour introduction could cover the project purpose, relevant samples, open conditions and the person responsible for follow-up. Avoid filling the agenda with every possible future collaboration. You can note other ideas without allowing them to displace the reason for the call."
